    IDS_HINT "Drop an audio file here\r\n\r\nTranscribe audio with timestamps and speaker labels.\r\nYou can also choose File > Add audio or Ctrl+O.\r\nChoose the model and quality in Settings > Settings, Transcription.\r\n\r\nThe file list and results are saved on this PC and restored when you reopen the app.\r\nRight-click a file for save, full copy, cancel, retranscribe, speaker names, or history removal.\r\nDeleting history keeps the original audio and exported files.\r\n\r\nIf models are missing, open Prepare models to download the required files.\r\nSupported input: M4A (AAC-LC / ALAC / HE-AAC), WAV (16-bit PCM, mono/stereo, 8–192 kHz), MP3 (MPEG-1/2 Layer III, mono/stereo), FLAC (native, 16/24-bit, mono/stereo, 8–192 kHz, known total samples).\r\nALAC: single audio track, version 0, 16/24-bit, mono/stereo, 8–48 kHz, known total samples. No edit list, encryption, fragmented container, or multiple tracks.\r\nHE-AAC v1: mono/stereo; v2: stereo; 44.1/48 kHz; a single audio track (explicit signaling, version 0). No edit list, encryption, fragmented container, external reference, or multiple tracks.\r\nTranscription and speaker separation support recordings over one hour, with no fixed recording-duration cap."
